# VIDEO-mode KEY frame byte-identity matrix, 72x88 q40, five synthetic
# content classes x twelve presets

date: 2026-09-23
host: lilith (WSL2 x86_64)
base: 64cc4645b + the key_min_sq fix — `pd0_pick_sb_partition_video_eval`
      hardcoded the key-frame `min_sq` to 8 on the claim that
      `pic_disallow_4x4` is 1 "at every preset this reaches", but
      `svt_aom_get_disallow_4x4_default` (enc_mode_config.c:8169) returns
      false at M0..M2, so C's PD0 evaluates 4x4 leaves on a key frame
      there and the port floored at 8x8. The inflated 8x8 rds cascaded
      upward and flipped PD0 split decisions (e.g. (0,0) 32x32 kept
      square at 43,582,215 vs split 43,616,078 where C split at
      43,462,085), which removed the 4x4 level from the PD1 refined scan
      and changed the committed tree on `gradient p0` (1341 vs 1320 B).

result: 60 / 60 byte-identical (0 diff, 0 broken) — the last open cell,
        `gradient p0`, closed. Regression gates same change:
        inter_byte_matrix 96/96 BOTH, issue9_knobs 36/36,
        bd10_video_gate 24/24, video_selfcheck 270/270,
        encoder tests 2603/2603.
